# Table Component Rules

## Overview
All tables must be rendered through a standard, reusable wrapper built on TanStack Table. First check the codebase for an existing wrapper; if one exists (e.g. `AppDataTable` at `@/components/DataTable`), use it. If none exists, create one named `AppDataTable` using `@tanstack/react-table` and place it under `components/` (e.g. `components/data-table.tsx`, kebab-case). Column definitions must be defined at module scope, never inside a component's render function.

## Rules

### 1. Find or Create `AppDataTable`
Before rendering a table, locate the existing standard table wrapper in the codebase. If present, use it for all table rendering. If absent, create `AppDataTable` (a TanStack Table wrapper) once and reuse it. Never import or use `useReactTable`, `flexRender`, `getCoreRowModel`, or raw TanStack Table components (`<Table>`, `<TableHeader>`, `<TableBody>`, `<TableRow>`, `<TableCell>`) directly — those are internal to the `AppDataTable` wrapper. Feature code imports only `AppDataTable`.

### 2. Column Definitions in Outer Scope
Column definitions must be defined outside the component scope as module-level `const` or a `createColumns()` factory function. Never define `ColumnDef<T>[]` inside a component render.

- **Simple tables** (no callbacks): export a `const columns: ColumnDef<T>[]` at module scope
- **Tables with actions**: use a `createColumns()` factory function exported from a dedicated `columns.ts` file

### 3. Hidable Columns
Tables must support column visibility toggling. `AppDataTable` provides a built-in "Columns" dropdown. Ensure every column has an explicit `id` property so it appears in the visibility menu.

### 4. Empty State
`AppDataTable` handles empty state implicitly via the `emptyState` prop which accepts `<EmptyStateContent>{...}</EmptyStateContent>`. When omitted, a default "No results" placeholder is shown. Callers must not add their own empty-state conditionals or inline "No results." text.

### 5. Currency Columns
Currency values must use `tabular-nums` and be aligned right. Put the currency symbol in the column header only — never in the cells.

- Header: `Amount (₦)`
- Cell: `1,250.00` (no `₦`)

## Code Snippets

### Column Definitions at Module Scope

```typescript
import type { ColumnDef } from "@tanstack/react-table";

type MyRow = {
  id: string;
  name: string;
  email: string | null;
};

const columns: ColumnDef<MyRow>[] = [
  { id: "sn", header: "S/N", cell: ({ row }) => row.index + 1 },
  { id: "name", header: "Name", accessorKey: "name" },
  { id: "email", header: "Email", accessorKey: "email" },
];
```

### createColumns Factory (with callbacks)

```typescript
// columns.ts
export function createColumns(actions: {
  onView: (id: string) => void;
}): ColumnDef<MyRow>[] {
  return [
    {
      id: "name",
      header: "Name",
      accessorKey: "name",
      cell: ({ row }) => (
        <button onClick={() => actions.onView(row.original.id)}>
          {row.getValue("name")}
        </button>
      ),
    },
    { id: "email", header: "Email", accessorKey: "email" },
  ];
}
```

### Usage with AppDataTable

```typescript
const cols = React.useMemo(() => createColumns({ onView: handleView }), []);

return (
  <AppDataTable
    columns={cols}
    data={rows}
    onRowClick={(row) => handleSelect(row.id)}
    emptyState={
      <EmptyStateContent>
        <EmptyStateTitle>No items found</EmptyStateTitle>
        <EmptyStateDescription>Try adjusting your filters.</EmptyStateDescription>
      </EmptyStateContent>
    }
  />
);
```

### Currency Columns

```typescript
const currency = (value: number) =>
  new Intl.NumberFormat("en-NG", { minimumFractionDigits: 2 }).format(value);

{
  id: "amount",
  header: "Amount (₦)", // symbol lives here only
  accessorKey: "amount",
  meta: { headerClassName: "text-right", cellClassName: "text-right tabular-nums" },
  cell: ({ row }) => currency(row.original.amount), // no symbol in the cell
}

// no meta support in the wrapper? use cell-level markup
cell: ({ row }) => (
  <span className="tabular-nums text-right">{currency(row.original.amount)}</span>
)
```

### Column Visibility Dropdown (built into AppDataTable)

```typescript
// DataTable.tsx — no action needed from callers
<DropdownMenu>
  <DropdownMenuTrigger asChild>
    <Button variant="outline" className="ml-auto">
      Columns <ChevronDown />
    </Button>
  </DropdownMenuTrigger>
  <DropdownMenuContent align="end">
    {table
      .getAllColumns()
      .filter((column) => column.getCanHide())
      .map((column) => (
        <DropdownMenuCheckboxItem
          key={column.id}
          className="capitalize"
          checked={column.getIsVisible()}
          onCheckedChange={(value) => column.toggleVisibility(!!value)}
        >
          {column.id}
        </DropdownMenuCheckboxItem>
      ))}
  </DropdownMenuContent>
</DropdownMenu>
```

## Bad Examples

```typescript
// ❌ Raw TanStack table setup inside component
const table = useReactTable({ data, columns, getCoreRowModel: getCoreRowModel() });
return (
  <Table>
    <TableHeader>...</TableHeader>
    <TableBody>{flexRender(...)}</TableBody>
  </Table>
);

// ❌ Column definitions inside component render
function MyTable() {
  const columns: ColumnDef<Row>[] = [...]; // wrong scope
  return <AppDataTable columns={columns} ... />;
}

// ❌ Caller handling empty state inline
{data.length === 0 && <p>No results</p>} // AppDataTable handles this

// ❌ Symbol repeated in every cell, proportional digits
cell: ({ row }) => <span>₦{row.original.amount}</span> // symbol belongs in header, add tabular-nums + text-right
```
